    "question": "Steve is building a bench for the playground and needs 6 lengths of wood that measure 4 feet and 2 lengths of wood that measure 2 feet. How many feet of wood does Steve need to buy?",
    "gold": "28",
    "answer": "Steve needs 6 lengths of 4 feet of wood or 6 x 4 = <<6*4=24>>24 feet of wood.\nHe also needs 2 lengths of 2 feet of wood or 2 x 2 = <<2*2=4>>4 feet of wood.\nAltogether, Steve needs 24 feet of wood + 4 feet of wood = <<24+4=28>>28 feet of wood.\n#### 28"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total amount of wood Steve needs to buy, we will calculate the total length of wood required for both the 4-foot lengths and the 2-foot lengths separately, and then sum these amounts.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total length of wood needed for the 4-foot lengths:\n\\[\n6 \\text{ lengths} \\times 4 \\text{ feet per length} = 24 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the total length of wood needed for the 2-foot lengths:\n\\[\n2 \\text{ lengths} \\times 2 \\text{ feet per length} = 4 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two amounts together to find the total length of wood Steve needs to buy:\n\\[\n24 \\text{ feet} + 4 \\text{ feet} = 28 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount of wood Steve needs to buy is \\boxed{28}.",
